        "subject": "LU-20861 socklnd: set bvec offset with bvec_iter_advance()",
        "message": "LU-20861 socklnd: set bvec offset with bvec_iter_advance()\n\nLinux commit b539aeacf8cc (\"block: rename bi_bvec_done\"), in\nv7.3-rc1, renamed bi_bvec_done to bi_offset, breaking the\ndesignated initializer in ksocknal_iter_for_each_range().\n\nUse bvec_iter_advance() to initialize the offset without depending\non the field name. Initialize bi_size to skip + bytes so advancing\nby skip preserves the original checksum range. This walk only runs\nfor the optional receive checksum, which is only sent on V2\nconnections.\n\nsocklnd_lib.c now compiles without warnings against v7.3-rc5\n(ktest mainline/ml); the build still fails elsewhere on the\nstrncpy() removal, see LU-20434. A userspace harness compiling\nthis function against bvec.h from v7.2 and v7.3 produced the same\nbyte ranges as the original over about a million generated cases.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5.5\nSigned-off-by: Chell Laszlo <pumpkinbiscuit@proton.me>\nChange-Id: Ia7224293a886f3dc3db14e8374e7e5d9379ed8a7\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69345\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Shaun Tancheff <shaun@tancheff.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
